/** @mainpage %Qore dataframe Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section dataframeintro dataframe Module Introduction

    The \c dataframe module provides a columnar DataFrame data structure for the
    <a href="../../lang/html/index.html">Qore programming language</a>, enabling
    typed, SQL-like data manipulation for enterprise data science workloads.

    Features:
    - Typed columns: \c float64 (Eigen3-backed), \c int64, \c string, \c bool, \c date
    - Null/missing value support with per-column null masks
    - SQL-like operations: select, filter, sort, groupby, join, valueCounts, nunique,
      pivot, melt, missing-data cleanup, and window functions
    - Dense column interop with \c buffer<T> and @ref Qore::SQL::ColumnarResult "ColumnarResult"
      for SQL and pipeline workloads
    - Native plugin-operator support: \c frame["column"] for columns,
      \c frame[row] for row hashes, \c frame[start..stop] for row slices, and
      \c frame[mask] for predicate masks
    - I/O: CSV (streaming reader), Parquet via Apache Arrow, database (Qore DBI)
    - ML integration: toMatrix/toVector/fromMatrix for zero-overhead ML feeding
    - Thread-safe with cooperative cancellation support

    To use this module, use \c "%requires dataframe" in your code.

